  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive): X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{細|ほそ}める\n- Intransitive counterpart: {細|ほそ}まる (to become narrow)\n\nUSAGE:\n⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{細|ほそ}める is read from context: squinting against light, or the warm, crinkled smile of someone looking at something dear (a child, a grandchild, a pet). In writing it is a set way to show affection.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{細|ほそ}める: to squint; to smile fondly\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{細|ほそ}めて⟦{喜|よろこ}ぶ→喜ぶ：01169_yorokobu⟧: to beam with delight",
